Kino: more half-open connections per torrent

The torrent library dials at most HalfOpenConnsPerTorrent peers at once
(default 25) and TorrServer never raised it. On a big swarm most dials wait
10-20 s for an answer, so new seeders were picked up slowly: on the Z9X a
45 Mbit/s BD-Remux sat at 15-26 Mbit/s with 25 of 25 half-open slots in use
and about 100 known peers. Allow 3/4 of the connection limit (at least 25).

 server/torr/btserver.go | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)
diff --git a/server/torr/btserver.go b/server/torr/btserver.go
--- a/server/torr/btserver.go
+++ b/server/torr/btserver.go
@@ -122,6 +122,11 @@
 	bt.config.HTTPUserAgent = userAgent
 	bt.config.ExtendedHandshakeClientVersion = cliVers
 	bt.config.EstablishedConnsPerTorrent = settings.BTsets.ConnectionsLimit
+	// Kino: dial more peers at once (library default 25), so a big swarm fills up quickly
+	bt.config.HalfOpenConnsPerTorrent = settings.BTsets.ConnectionsLimit * 3 / 4
+	if bt.config.HalfOpenConnsPerTorrent < 25 {
+		bt.config.HalfOpenConnsPerTorrent = 25
+	}
 	bt.config.TotalHalfOpenConns = 500
 	// Encryption/Obfuscation
 	bt.config.EncryptionPolicy = torrent.EncryptionPolicy{ //	OE
